      "text": "4,919.\n</think>\n\nTo find the **Product of 52 and 87**, follow these easy steps:\n\n### Step 1: Break Down the Numbers\nIt's often easier to multiply larger numbers by breaking them into smaller, more manageable parts.\n\n\\[\n52 \\times 87 = (50 + 2) \\times (80 + 7)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Use the Distributive Property\nApply the distributive property to multiply each part:\n\n\\[\n(50 + 2) \\times (80 + 7) = 50 \\times 80 + 50 \\times 7 + 2 \\times 80 + 2 \\times 7\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate Each Part\n\n1. **Multiply 50 by 80:**\n   \\[\n   50 \\times 80 = 4,000\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Multiply 50 by 7:**\n   \\[\n   50 \\times 7 = 350\n   \\]\n   \n3. **Multiply 2 by 80:**\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 80 = 160\n   \\]\n   \n4. **Multiply 2 by 7:**\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 7 = 14\n   \\]\n\n### Step 4: Add All the Parts Together\n\n\\[\n4,000 + 350 + 160 + 14 = 4,524\n\\]\n\n### Final Answer\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4,\\!524}\n\\]",
